# Central exceptions for the image scan in .github/workflows/build-dev-images.yml
# (`trivy image`, gate policy: --ignore-unfixed --severity HIGH,CRITICAL).
#
# Every entry needs two comment lines above it, and an entry without them is a
# review comment, not a merge:
#
#   # why: <what makes this finding not apply to these images>
#   # until: YYYY-MM-DD -- <what happens on that date>
#   CVE-0000-00000
#
# The date is a convention, not a mechanism: trivy's plain .trivyignore has no
# expiry field, so nothing enforces it — that is precisely why it has to be
# written down and re-read. An entry past its date is either renewed with a
# fresh reason or deleted; "it was here when I got here" is not a reason.
#
# Scope: these images are DEVELOPMENT and CI images. That is an argument for
# some exceptions (a CVE reachable only through a service nothing here runs) and
# for none at all in the direction people usually reach for — a dev image that
# eleven repos boot on every push is not an image where an unaudited exception
# is cheap.
#
# Nothing is excused right now, which is the state to keep.
